            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42306",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Moby is an open source container framework. In Docker Engine prior to  ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Moby is an open source container framework. In Docker Engine prior to version 29.5.1, Docker Daemon versions 28.5.2 and prior, and Moby Daemon prior to version 2.0.0-beta.14, a race condition during docker cp mount setup allows a malicious container to redirect a bind mount target to an arbitrary host path, potentially overwriting host files or causing denial of service. This issue has been patched in Docker Engine version 29.5.1 and Moby Daemon version 2.0.0-beta.14."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42306",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-42306\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/docker/docker\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-42306](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42306)\nMoby is an open source container framework. In Docker Engine prior to version 29.5.1, Docker Daemon versions 28.5.2 and prior, and Moby Daemon prior to version 2.0.0-beta.14, a race condition during docker cp mount setup allows a malicious container to redirect a bind mount target to an arbitrary host path, potentially overwriting host files or causing denial of service. This issue has been patched in Docker Engine version 29.5.1 and Moby Daemon version 2.0.0-beta.14.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-42306**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/docker/docker||[CVE-2026-42306](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42306)|\n\nMoby is an open source container framework. In Docker Engine prior to version 29.5.1, Docker Daemon versions 28.5.2 and prior, and Moby Daemon prior to version 2.0.0-beta.14, a race condition during docker cp mount setup allows a malicious container to redirect a bind mount target to an arbitrary host path, potentially overwriting host files or causing denial of service. This issue has been patched in Docker Engine version 29.5.1 and Moby Daemon version 2.0.0-beta.14."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.2,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:R/S:C/C:N/I:H/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.2",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-33997",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "moby: docker: github.com/moby/moby: Moby: Privilege validation bypass during plugin installation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Moby is an open source container framework. Prior to version 29.3.1, a security vulnerability has been detected that allows plugins privilege validation to be bypassed during docker plugin install. Due to an error in the daemon's privilege comparison logic, the daemon may incorrectly accept a privilege set that differs from the one approved by the user. Plugins that request exactly one privilege are also affected, because no comparison is performed at all. This issue has been patched in version 29.3.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-33997",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-33997\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/docker/docker\nFixed Version: 29.3.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-33997](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-33997)\nMoby is an open source container framework. Prior to version 29.3.1, a security vulnerability has been detected that allows plugins privilege validation to be bypassed during docker plugin install. Due to an error in the daemon's privilege comparison logic, the daemon may incorrectly accept a privilege set that differs from the one approved by the user. Plugins that request exactly one privilege are also affected, because no comparison is performed at all. This issue has been patched in version 29.3.1.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-33997**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/docker/docker|29.3.1|[CVE-2026-33997](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-33997)|\n\nMoby is an open source container framework. Prior to version 29.3.1, a security vulnerability has been detected that allows plugins privilege validation to be bypassed during docker plugin install. Due to an error in the daemon's privilege comparison logic, the daemon may incorrectly accept a privilege set that differs from the one approved by the user. Plugins that request exactly one privilege are also affected, because no comparison is performed at all. This issue has been patched in version 29.3.1."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.8,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.8",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41568",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/docker/docker: github.com/moby/moby: Moby: Denial of Service via race condition in docker cp mount setup"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Moby is an open source container framework. In Docker Engine prior to version 29.5.1, Docker Daemon versions 28.5.2 and prior, and Moby Daemon prior to version 2.0.0-beta.14, a race condition during docker cp mount setup allows a malicious container to create empty files or directories at arbitrary absolute paths on the host filesystem. This issue has been patched in Docker Engine version 29.5.1 and Moby Daemon version 2.0.0-beta.14."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41568",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41568\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/docker/docker\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-41568](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41568)\nMoby is an open source container framework. In Docker Engine prior to version 29.5.1, Docker Daemon versions 28.5.2 and prior, and Moby Daemon prior to version 2.0.0-beta.14, a race condition during docker cp mount setup allows a malicious container to create empty files or directories at arbitrary absolute paths on the host filesystem. This issue has been patched in Docker Engine version 29.5.1 and Moby Daemon version 2.0.0-beta.14.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41568**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/docker/docker||[CVE-2026-41568](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41568)|\n\nMoby is an open source container framework. In Docker Engine prior to version 29.5.1, Docker Daemon versions 28.5.2 and prior, and Moby Daemon prior to version 2.0.0-beta.14, a race condition during docker cp mount setup allows a malicious container to create empty files or directories at arbitrary absolute paths on the host filesystem. This issue has been patched in Docker Engine version 29.5.1 and Moby Daemon version 2.0.0-beta.14."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:R/S:C/C:N/I:L/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.0",
                "tags": [
